  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Turn and go home – 1v1 chase game",
  "description": "A narrow rectangle, about 10 × 3 metres, with two lines side by side at one short end. One line has balls, the other chases. A cone two to three metres in marks where the carrier may turn at the earliest and where the chaser may take the ball at the earliest. Carrier A heads for the far end, turns after the cone and tries to carry the ball back to the start. Chaser B tries to stop the turn and ideally win the ball. Then both swap to the other line.\n\nPoints for A: 1 point for keeping the ball until the turn, 1 point for turning and reaching the end with the ball. Points for B: 2 points for winning the ball before A turns, 1 point for stopping A from reaching the end. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Which way is easiest to turn? Try both."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Turn with your body between the chaser and the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Chaser: when is it hardest for the player turning?"
    }
  ],
